          "Maintain active engagement with the African American constituency: at 42.46%, this is the district's largest demographic bloc and the foundation of Democratic strength, but unopposed status should not reduce focus on the specific economic pressures facing Black households — healthcare access, job quality, and wealth-building barriers are the issues that sustain political trust.",
          "Do not treat the White and Hispanic communities (53% combined) as secondary: these constituencies warrant specific constituent attention, not absorption into a broader 'other' category — engagement on economic mobility, small business support, and community services prevents future challengers from exploiting perceived neglect.",
          "Interpret unopposed status as a governance opportunity, not a permission to disengage: the most durable political position is built on active constituent service and specific legislative deliverables on housing, healthcare, and economic security — not on assumptions that party registration creates permanent electoral safety."
