          { name: "Culture war issues and social divisiveness", tag: "avoid", why: "A median age of 39.3 and college-educated population of 46.6% suggest voters prioritize pragmatic governance over culture-war positioning. The 58% Democratic result indicates the district rewards competence-focused messaging over ideological polarization. Candidates should avoid nationally-driven culture issues in favor of district-specific quality-of-life concerns where they can credibly claim effectiveness." }
