          "Recognize the 45% opposition as strategically significant: in a district with this income level and education profile, 45% Democratic support is not a fringe but a substantial constituency of affluent, educated voters actively choosing the other party — understand specifically why they did and offer concrete answers rather than assuming the 55% Republican margin will hold without active engagement.",
          "Include the renter minority in your framing without making it the focus: while 90% of the district is homeowners, the 9.9% renter population exists and deserves visible acknowledgment; a candidate whose language and messaging entirely excludes renters signals exclusionary governance and sacrifices credibility with the educated, civic-minded homeowner majority who value inclusive community."
