          "Engage Black community on economic security and legislative delivery: at 41.21%, the Black plurality is the district's demographic foundation, but the unopposed 2022 victory means the community's specific concerns around healthcare access, employment opportunity, and educational outcomes have not been tested electorally; building authentic constituent relationships around material needs, not racial solidarity alone, is the foundation for durable Black voter support.",
